commit bb45fb2f47d10690f0f36c3bfb283ca610be45d3 (origin/yuxzhang/canon-zero-tim)
Author: yuxuandexter <yuz165@ucsd.edu>
Date:   Wed Aug 19 07:13:40 2026 +0000
    Preserve the profiler postflight when markers are absent
    
    The exact-step parser ran under set -euo pipefail, so a capture-off run or a missing profiler marker exited during command substitution before the intended SUMMARY and RED/GREEN classifier could run. Treat an absent marker as an empty parsed step and let the existing count and exact-step gates classify it. The tradeoff is only a less immediate shell exit; missing markers remain fatal when capture is requested and remain valid when P51_CAPTURE=0. Host controls cover absent, correct 2-to-3, and wrong-step inputs; p54final_20260819 remains the target artifact.
commit 818066d73d7f623a6e18e3abb9eb3a05e95c972f
Date:   Wed Aug 19 07:03:14 2026 +0000
    Register the P54 official-stack work in the package registries
    FLAGS.md gains CANON_PERF_TRACE_DIR with its default-empty NoopTracer
    semantics and the inventory count moves to 299. EVIDENCE.md's run index
    gains the p54final row with the three artifact SHAs. THREADS.md's perf
    row and the perf task state now describe the official stack, the exact
    window step numbers, and where the single authoritative run recipe
    lives.
commit 0e176f8da0494d5ffd1d5e9aaf42c4ae75580353
Date:   Wed Aug 19 07:02:09 2026 +0000
    Rewrite the profiling runbook around the official stack
    Two instruments, one run: the tunix.perf v2 semantic timeline and the
    official Profiler's device capture, each with its artifact names, sizes,
    and viewing path. The knob table carries the tracer-level evidence, the
    green criteria match the official profiler's log lines including the
    exact step numbers, and a section spells out what running the demo
    directly on another host must set -- the gap the 64MB host-only incident
    fell through. The cross-host mesh note reflects the land-and-revert of
    the explicit-host remedies and points at the incident report's per-host
    table instead of a footgun entry that never landed.
commit dc6bf1fd6f28c6dcda218be2f02db005549b7b8f
Date:   Wed Aug 19 07:01:45 2026 +0000
    Record the host dependence without endorsing the reverted remedies
    The embedder out_sharding change and the FL_SHARED_MESH=1,4 advice landed
    as 6daec65e and were reverted in e26b70b3, so the report now states the
    land-and-revert history, pins the per-host settings that the two mirror
    incidents actually established, and marks explicit-mesh-engine support as
    open work with a pointer to the unpushed helper rather than a claim that
    anything is fixed on this branch.
commit 8a6e025b3ddda659ce59d4d284f0b779ae8dceb8
Date:   Wed Aug 19 07:01:15 2026 +0000
    Route one-host profiling through the official tunix.perf stack
    The framework was in the branch all along -- tunix/perf with the v2
    tracer, spans already sitting in the agentic learner, the per-global-step
    export call, and tunix.sft.profiler's window class -- only nothing fed
    it: the demo never passed perf_config, so every span hit a NoopTracer,
    and a hand-rolled learner hook duplicated what ProfilerOptions already
    expresses.
    The demo now builds PerfMetricsConfig from the deepscaler pattern
    (experimental PerfMetricsExport.from_cluster_config with a trace_dir)
    whenever CANON_PERF_TRACE_DIR is set, which turns the existing spans into
    perfetto_trace_v2_<ts>.pb semantic timelines. The learner keeps its
    single call site but the hand-rolled start/stop state machine is replaced
    by the official Profiler; it stays learner-driven because the G6
    segmented update path never enters PeftTrainer.train(), where the
    trainer-level activation lives, and the window must cover the rollout
    anyway. The skip >= 1 guard survives: the official class quietly never
    triggers on a skip of zero for the same off-by-one the old hook had.
    Tracer levels ride ProfilerOptions, still pinned python=0 / host=1 by
    the vehicle: the official defaults (2/1) measurably crowd every device
    plane out of the capture on this image. The vehicle passes the trace
    dir, requires the v2 trace in its gate, and checks the profiler's own
    absl lines for the exact start and stop step numbers -- presence counts
    alone would pass a window that opened at the wrong step. Controls: the
    step parse reads 2/3 from the verified run's log, and a synthetic
    wrong-step log goes red.
    Verified on the one-host vehicle (p54final_20260819): 3/3 steps, 51/51
    alignment reports all-zero, window opened at step 2 and closed at step 3,
    xplane 1852MB, trace.json.gz 39MB, semantic v2 trace 19.9KB with 503
    packets / 480 track events across the Host-Rollout / Host-Main /
    Actor-Reference-Rollout-Cluster tracks.
