commit 11273a9e93a64af7fbc58a8e5be543baab8cd8e0
Date:   Thu Aug 20 00:51:27 2026 +0000
    Revert "Add v2 training-phase spans on the G6 segmented update path"
    This reverts commit 472df1946a986e8734bb18edbaf46eae1a70d8ab.
    The three spans made the semantic timeline unreadable instead of richer.
    All of them passed all_devices and nested inside each other, and the
    trace writer answered by scattering them: peft_train landed on the
    device-cluster track AND on per-device tracks between rollout slices,
    while the two custom-named inner spans spilled onto an extra auxiliary
    lane (p55c track census: uuid=1200002 / 1300002 carry only
    segmented_value_and_grad + gradient_commit mixed with rollouts). In the
    perfetto UI that renders as one smeared bar. The official usage
    (peft_trainer.py:1835) is flat -- one PEFT_TRAIN span per unit of work,
    official vocabulary only, async_end([...]) for device attribution, no
    nesting -- and the metrics documentation prescribes no custom span
    names. A rewrite following that shape exactly comes as its own CL; the
    G6 update-entry anchor for the device capture stays, it never depended
    on the span.
    The update-entry hook keeps its call site; only the span wrapper around
    the G6 update call is gone.
